{"id":"mahabharata-3-083","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":83,"title":"त्र्यशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 83 · The end of Pulastya's list","summary":{"en":"Pulastya completes his list with the fords of the south and west and declares that pilgrimage, open to the poor, surpasses costly sacrifices. Narada tells Yudhishthira that he too should make the pilgrimage with Lomasha, and Yudhishthira resolves to go.","kn":"ದಕ್ಷಿಣ ಪಶ್ಚಿಮದ ತೀರ್ಥಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಪುಲಸ್ತ್ಯರು ಪಟ್ಟಿಯನ್ನು ಮುಗಿಸಿ, ಬಡವರಿಗೂ ಸಾಧ್ಯವಾದ ತೀರ್ಥಯಾತ್ರೆ ದುಬಾರಿ ಯಜ್ಞಗಳನ್ನು ಮೀರುತ್ತದೆ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾರೆ. ನೀನೂ ಲೋಮಶರೊಂದಿಗೆ ತೀರ್ಥಯಾತ್ರೆ ಮಾಡು ಎಂದು ನಾರದರು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಹೊರಡಲು ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पुलस्त्य दक्षिण और पश्चिम के तीर्थों के साथ सूची पूरी करते हैं और कहते हैं कि निर्धनों के लिए भी सुलभ तीर्थयात्रा महँगे यज्ञों से बढ़कर है। नारद युधिष्ठिर से लोमश के साथ तीर्थयात्रा करने को कहते हैं, और युधिष्ठिर जाने का निश्चय करते हैं।","te":"దక్షిణ, పశ్చిమ తీర్థాలతో పులస్త్యుడు జాబితా ముగించి, పేదలకు కూడా సాధ్యమైన తీర్థయాత్ర ఖరీదైన యజ్ఞాలను మించుతుందంటాడు. నీవూ లోమశునితో తీర్థయాత్ర చేయమని నారదుడు చెబుతాడు, యుధిష్ఠిరుడు బయలుదేరడానికి నిశ్చయిస్తాడు.","ta":"தெற்கு, மேற்குத் தீர்த்தங்களுடன் புலஸ்த்யர் பட்டியலை முடித்து, ஏழைகளுக்கும் இயலும் தீர்த்தயாத்திரை செலவுமிக்க யாகங்களை விஞ்சும் என்கிறார். நீரும் லோமஶருடன் தீர்த்தயாத்திரை செய்யுமாறு நாரதர் சொல்ல, யுதிஷ்டிரர் புறப்படத் தீர்மானிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ദക്ഷിണദിക്കിലെയും പശ്ചിമദിക്കിലെയും തീർത്ഥങ്ങൾ പറഞ്ഞ് പുലസ്ത്യൻ പട്ടിക പൂർത്തിയാക്കുന്നു; ദരിദ്രർക്കും തുറന്നിട്ടുള്ള തീർത്ഥയാത്ര വിലയേറിയ യാഗങ്ങളെക്കാൾ മികച്ചതാണെന്ന് പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു. ലോമശനോടൊപ്പം തീർത്ഥയാത്ര നടത്താൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനോട് നാരദൻ പറയുന്നു; യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പോകാൻ തീരുമാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.83; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"पुलस्त्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Pulastya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथ संध्यां समासाद्य संवेद्यं तीर्थमुत्तमम् ।\nउपस्पृश्य नरो विद्वान्भवेन्नास्त्यत्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching Sandhya and the excellent ford Samvedya, a man who rinses there becomes learned, without doubt."}},{"n":2,"text":"रामस्य च प्रसादेन तीर्थं राजन्कृतं पुरा ।\nतल्लोहित्यं समासाद्य विन्द्याद्बहु सुवर्णकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By Rama's grace a ford was made there long ago, O king; reaching that Lauhitya, one gains much gold."}},{"n":3,"text":"करतोयां समासाद्य त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति कृते पैतामहे विधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the Karatoya and fasting three nights, a man gains the horse sacrifice, as laid down by the Grandfather's rule."}},{"n":4,"text":"गङ्गायास्त्वथ राजेन्द्र सागरस्य च संगमे ।\nअश्वमेधं दशगुणं प्रवदन्ति मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the confluence of the Ganga and the sea, king of kings, the wise say one gains ten times the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":5,"text":"गङ्गायास्त्वपरं द्वीपं प्राप्य यः स्नाति भारत ।\nत्रिरात्रोपोषितो राजन्सर्वकामानवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who reaches the farther island of the Ganga and bathes there, O Bharata, fasting three nights, O king, obtains all desires."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततो वैतरणीं गत्वा नदीं पापप्रमोचनीम् ।\nविरजं तीर्थमासाद्य विराजति यथा शशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, going to the Vaitarani, the river that frees from sin, and reaching Virajatirtha, one shines like the moon."}},{"n":7,"text":"प्रभवेच्च कुले पुण्ये सर्वपापं व्यपोहति ।\nगोसहस्रफलं लब्ध्वा पुनाति च कुलं नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is born in a holy family, shakes off all sin, gains the fruit of a thousand cows and purifies his family."}},{"n":8,"text":"शोणस्य ज्योतिरथ्याश्च संगमे निवसञ्शुचिः ।\nतर्पयित्वा पितॄन्देवानग्निष्टोमफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Staying pure at the confluence of the Shona and the Jyotiratha and offering water to ancestors and gods, one gains the fruit of the Agnishtoma."}},{"n":9,"text":"शोणस्य नर्मदायाश्च प्रभवे कुरुनन्दन ।\nवंशगुल्म उपस्पृश्य वाजिमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joy of the Kurus, at the source of the Shona and Narmada, rinsing at Vamshagulma, one gains the fruit of the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":10,"text":"ऋषभं तीर्थमासाद्य कोशलायां नराधिप ।\nवाजपेयमवाप्नोति त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Rishabhatirtha in Koshala, ruler of men, a man who fasts three nights gains the Vajapeya."}},{"n":11,"text":"कोशलायां समासाद्य कालतीर्थ उपस्पृशेत् ।\nवृषभैकादशफलं लभते नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Koshala and rinsing at Kalatirtha, one gains, without doubt, the fruit of giving eleven bulls."}},{"n":12,"text":"पुष्पवत्यामुपस्पृश्य त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nगोसहस्रफलं विन्द्यात्कुलं चैव समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rinsing at Pushpavati and fasting three nights, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows and uplifts one's family."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततो बदरिकातीर्थे स्नात्वा प्रयतमानसः ।\nदीर्घमायुरवाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, bathing at Badarikatirtha with composed mind, one gains long life and goes to heaven."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततो महेन्द्रमासाद्य जामदग्न्यनिषेवितम् ।\nरामतीर्थे नरः स्नात्वा वाजिमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching Mahendra, frequented by Jamadagni's son, and bathing at Ramatirtha, a man gains the fruit of the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":15,"text":"मतङ्गस्य तु केदारस्तत्रैव कुरुनन्दन ।\nतत्र स्नात्वा नरो राजन्गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too is Matanga's Kedara, joy of the Kurus; bathing there, O king, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":16,"text":"श्रीपर्वतं समासाद्य नदीतीर उपस्पृशेत् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Shriparvata and rinsing on the riverbank, one gains the horse sacrifice and goes to heaven."}},{"n":17,"text":"श्रीपर्वते महादेवो देव्या सह महाद्युतिः ।\nन्यवसत्परमप्रीतो ब्रह्मा च त्रिदशैर्वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On Shriparvata, Mahadeva of great radiance lived with the Goddess, greatly pleased, and Brahma too, surrounded by the gods."}},{"n":18,"text":"तत्र देवह्रदे स्नात्वा शुचिः प्रयतमानसः ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति परां सिद्धिं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing there at the Devahrada, pure and with composed mind, one gains the horse sacrifice and attains great success."}},{"n":19,"text":"ऋषभं पर्वतं गत्वा पाण्ड्येषु सुरपूजितम् ।\nवाजपेयमवाप्नोति नाकपृष्ठे च मोदते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Mount Rishabha among the Pandyas, honoured by the gods, one gains the Vajapeya and rejoices in the highest heaven."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततो गच्छेत कावेरीं वृतामप्सरसां गणैः ।\nतत्र स्नात्वा नरो राजन्गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to the Kaveri, attended by hosts of apsaras; bathing there, O king, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततस्तीरे समुद्रस्य कन्यातीर्थ उपस्पृशेत् ।\nतत्रोपस्पृश्य राजेन्द्र सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then on the seashore one should rinse at Kanyatirtha; rinsing there, king of kings, one is freed from all sins."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथ गोकर्णमासाद्य त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुतम् ।\nसमुद्रमध्ये राजेन्द्र सर्वलोकनमस्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching Gokarna, famed in the three worlds, in the middle of the sea, O king of kings, honoured by all the worlds,"}},{"n":23,"text":"यत्र ब्रह्मादयो देवा ऋषयश्च तपोधनाः ।\nभूतयक्षपिशाचाश्च किंनराः समहोरगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"where Brahma and the other gods, ascetic sages, bhutas, yakshas, pishachas, kinnaras and great serpents,"}},{"n":24,"text":"सिद्धचारणगन्धर्वा मानुषाः पन्नगास्तथा ।\nसरितः सागराः शैला उपासन्त उमापतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"siddhas, charanas, gandharvas, humans, nagas, rivers, oceans and mountains worship the lord of Uma,"}},{"n":25,"text":"तत्रेशानं समभ्यर्च्य त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nदशाश्वमेधमाप्नोति गाणपत्यं च विन्दति ।\nउष्य द्वादशरात्रं तु कृतात्मा भवते नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"worshipping Ishana there and fasting three nights, a man gains ten horse sacrifices and leadership of Shiva's host. Staying twelve nights, he becomes accomplished in self."}},{"n":26,"text":"तत एव तु गायत्र्याः स्थानं त्रैलोक्यविश्रुतम् ।\nत्रिरात्रमुषितस्तत्र गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From there one goes to the place of Gayatri, famed in the three worlds; staying three nights there, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":27,"text":"निदर्शनं च प्रत्यक्षं ब्राह्मणानां नराधिप ।\nगायत्रीं पठते यस्तु योनिसंकरजस्तथा ।\nगाथा वा गीतिका वापि तस्य संपद्यते नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"A direct proof for brahmins, ruler of men: even one born of a mixed womb who recites the Gayatri there finds a gatha or song come to him."}},{"n":28,"text":"संवर्तस्य तु विप्रर्षेर्वापीमासाद्य दुर्लभाम् ।\nरूपस्य भागी भवति सुभगश्चैव जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the very rare stepwell of the brahmin sage Samvarta, one gains beauty and is born fortunate."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो वेण्णां समासाद्य तर्पयेत्पितृदेवताः ।\nमयूरहंससंयुक्तं विमानं लभते नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching the Venna and offering water to ancestors and gods, a man gains a celestial chariot yoked with peacocks and swans."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततो गोदावरीं प्राप्य नित्यं सिद्धनिषेविताम् ।\nगवामयमवाप्नोति वासुकेर्लोकमाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching the Godavari, always frequented by siddhas, one gains the Gavamaya and reaches Vasuki's world."}},{"n":31,"text":"वेण्णायाः संगमे स्नात्वा वाजपेयफलं लभेत् ।\nवरदासंगमे स्नात्वा गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at the confluence of the Venna one gains the fruit of the Vajapeya; bathing at the confluence of the Varada one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":32,"text":"ब्रह्मस्थानं समासाद्य त्रिरात्रमुषितो नरः ।\nगोसहस्रफलं विन्देत्स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Brahmasthana and staying three nights there, a man gains the fruit of a thousand cows and goes to heaven."}},{"n":33,"text":"कुशप्लवनमासाद्य ब्रह्मचारी समाहितः ।\nत्रिरात्रमुषितः स्नात्वा अश्वमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Kushaplavana, a celibate with composed mind who stays three nights and bathes there gains the fruit of the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततो देवह्रदे रम्ये कृष्णवेण्णाजलोद्भवे ।\nजातिमात्रह्रदे चैव तथा कन्याश्रमे नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at the lovely Devahrada, arising from the waters of the Krishnavenna, and at Jatimatrahrada and Kanyashrama, O king,"}},{"n":35,"text":"यत्र क्रतुशतैरिष्ट्वा देवराजो दिवं गतः ।\nअग्निष्टोमशतं विन्देद्गमनादेव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"where the king of the gods went to heaven after performing a hundred sacrifices, one gains a hundred Agnishtomas merely by going there, O Bharata."}},{"n":36,"text":"सर्वदेवह्रदे स्नात्वा गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ।\nजातिमात्रह्रदे स्नात्वा भवेज्जातिस्मरो नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Sarvadevahrada one gains the fruit of a thousand cows; bathing at Jatimatrahrada, a man comes to remember his past births."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततोऽवाप्य महापुण्यां पयोष्णीं सरितां वराम् ।\nपितृदेवार्चनरतो गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching the very holy Payoshni, best of rivers, and devoted to honouring ancestors and gods, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":38,"text":"दण्डकारण्यमासाद्य महाराज उपस्पृशेत् ।\nगोसहस्रफलं तत्र स्नातमात्रस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Dandakaranya, great king, one should rinse; by merely bathing there, O Bharata, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":39,"text":"शरभङ्गाश्रमं गत्वा शुकस्य च महात्मनः ।\nन दुर्गतिमवाप्नोति पुनाति च कुलं नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to the hermitage of Sharabhanga and to that of the great soul Shuka, one meets no evil fate and purifies one's family."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततः शूर्पारकं गच्छेज्जामदग्न्यनिषेवितम् ।\nरामतीर्थे नरः स्नात्वा विन्द्याद्बहु सुवर्णकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to Shurparaka, frequented by Jamadagni's son; bathing at Ramatirtha, one gains much gold."}},{"n":41,"text":"सप्तगोदावरे स्नात्वा नियतो नियताशनः ।\nमहत्पुण्यमवाप्नोति देवलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Saptagodavara, restrained and with restrained diet, one gains great merit and goes to the gods' world."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततो देवपथं गच्छेन्नियतो नियताशनः ।\nदेवसत्रस्य यत्पुण्यं तदवाप्नोति मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, restrained and with restrained diet, one should go to Devapatha; a man gains the merit of the Devasatra sacrifice."}},{"n":43,"text":"तुङ्गकारण्यमासाद्य ब्रह्मचारी जितेन्द्रियः ।\nवेदानध्यापयत्तत्र ऋषिः सारस्वतः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Tungakaranya, a celibate who has mastered his senses: there in the past the sage Sarasvata taught the Vedas."}},{"n":44,"text":"तत्र वेदान्प्रनष्टांस्तु मुनेरङ्गिरसः सुतः ।\nउपविष्टो महर्षीणामुत्तरीयेषु भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the son of the muni Angiras, seated on the upper garments of great sages, restored the Vedas that had been lost, O Bharata."}},{"n":45,"text":"ओंकारेण यथान्यायं सम्यगुच्चारितेन च ।\nयेन यत्पूर्वमभ्यस्तं तत्तस्य समुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the syllable Om, correctly pronounced as it should be, whatever each man had studied before came back to him."}},{"n":46,"text":"ऋषयस्तत्र देवाश्च वरुणोऽग्निः प्रजापतिः ।\nहरिर्नारायणो देवो महादेवस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sages there and the gods, Varuna, Agni, Prajapati, the god Hari Narayana and likewise Mahadeva,"}},{"n":47,"text":"पितामहश्च भगवान्देवैः सह महाद्युतिः ।\nभृगुं नियोजयामास याजनार्थे महाद्युतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the blessed Grandfather of great radiance, with the gods, appointed the radiant Bhrigu as officiating priest."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततः स चक्रे भगवानृषीणां विधिवत्तदा ।\nसर्वेषां पुनराधानं विधिदृष्टेन कर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the blessed Bhrigu duly performed for all the sages the re-establishment of the sacred fires, by the rite laid down."}},{"n":49,"text":"आज्यभागेन वै तत्र तर्पितास्तु यथाविधि ।\nदेवास्त्रिभुवणं याता ऋषयश्च यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the gods were satisfied by the share of ghee in the proper way, and went to the three worlds, and the sages as they pleased."}},{"n":50,"text":"तदरण्यं प्रविष्टस्य तुङ्गकं राजसत्तम ।\nपापं प्रणश्यते सर्वं स्त्रियो वा पुरुषस्य वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who enters that Tungaka forest, best of kings, all sin of woman or man is destroyed."}},{"n":51,"text":"तत्र मासं वसेद्धीरो नियतो नियताशनः ।\nब्रह्मलोकं व्रजेद्राजन्पुनीते च कुलं नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A steadfast man should stay a month there, restrained and with restrained diet; he goes to Brahma's world, O king, and purifies his family."}},{"n":52,"text":"मेधाविकं समासाद्य पितॄन्देवांश्च तर्पयेत् ।\nअग्निष्टोममवाप्नोति स्मृतिं मेधां च विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Medhavika and offering water to ancestors and gods, one gains the Agnishtoma, and also memory and intelligence."}},{"n":53,"text":"ततः कालंजरं गत्वा पर्वतं लोकविश्रुतम् ।\nतत्र देवह्रदे स्नात्वा गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, going to Mount Kalanjara, famed in the world, and bathing at the Devahrada there, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":54,"text":"आत्मानं साधयेत्तत्र गिरौ कालंजरे नृप ।\nस्वर्गलोके महीयेत नरो नास्त्यत्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should perfect oneself on that mountain Kalanjara, O king; a man is honoured in heaven, without doubt."}},{"n":55,"text":"ततो गिरिवरश्रेष्ठे चित्रकूटे विशां पते ।\nमन्दाकिनीं समासाद्य नदीं पापप्रमोचनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of the people, on Chitrakuta, best of mountains, reaching the Mandakini, the river that frees from sin,"}},{"n":56,"text":"तत्राभिषेकं कुर्वाणः पितृदेवार्चने रतः ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति गतिं च परमां व्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"one should bathe there, devoted to honouring ancestors and gods; one gains the horse sacrifice and goes to the highest goal."}},{"n":57,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र भर्तृस्थानमनुत्तमम् ।\nयत्र देवो महासेनो नित्यं संनिहितो नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to the unsurpassed Bhartristhana, where the god Mahasena is always present, O king."}},{"n":58,"text":"पुमांस्तत्र नरश्रेष्ठ गमनादेव सिध्यति ।\nकोटितीर्थे नरः स्नात्वा गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man there attains success merely by going, best of men; bathing at Kotitirtha one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":59,"text":"प्रदक्षिणमुपावृत्य ज्येष्ठस्थानं व्रजेन्नरः ।\nअभिगम्य महादेवं विराजति यथा शशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"After circling it, a man should go to Jyeshthasthana; going to Mahadeva there he shines like the moon."}},{"n":60,"text":"तत्र कूपो महाराज विश्रुतो भरतर्षभ ।\nसमुद्रास्तत्र चत्वारो निवसन्ति युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a well there, great king, best of the Bharatas, famed; four oceans dwell there, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":61,"text":"तत्रोपस्पृश्य राजेन्द्र कृत्वा चापि प्रदक्षिणम् ।\nनियतात्मा नरः पूतो गच्छेत परमां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rinsing there, king of kings, and circling it, a self-controlled man becomes pure and reaches the highest goal."}},{"n":62,"text":"ततो गच्छेत्कुरुश्रेष्ठ शृङ्गवेरपुरं महत् ।\nयत्र तीर्णो महाराज रामो दाशरथिः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, best of the Kurus, one should go to the great Shringaverapura, where Rama son of Dasharatha once crossed."}},{"n":63,"text":"गङ्गायां तु नरः स्नात्वा ब्रह्मचारी समाहितः ।\nविधूतपाप्मा भवति वाजपेयं च विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A celibate with composed mind who bathes in the Ganga there has his sin shaken off and gains the Vajapeya."}},{"n":64,"text":"अभिगम्य महादेवमभ्यर्च्य च नराधिप ।\nप्रदक्षिणमुपावृत्य गाणपत्यमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Mahadeva and worshipping him, ruler of men, and circling him, one gains leadership of Shiva's host."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र प्रयागमृषिसंस्तुतम् ।\nयत्र ब्रह्मादयो देवा दिशश्च सदिगीश्वराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to Prayaga, praised by sages, where Brahma and the other gods, the directions with their guardians,"}},{"n":66,"text":"लोकपालाश्च साध्याश्च नैरृताः पितरस्तथा ।\nसनत्कुमारप्रमुखास्तथैव परमर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the world-guardians, Sadhyas, Nairritas and ancestors, and the great sages led by Sanatkumara,"}},{"n":67,"text":"अङ्गिरःप्रमुखाश्चैव तथा ब्रह्मर्षयोऽपरे ।\nतथा नागाः सुपर्णाश्च सिद्धाश्चक्रचरास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"others led by Angiras, the brahmin sages, nagas, suparnas, siddhas and those who travel with the wheel,"}},{"n":68,"text":"सरितः सागराश्चैव गन्धर्वाप्सरसस्तथा ।\nहरिश्च भगवानास्ते प्रजापतिपुरस्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"rivers and oceans, gandharvas and apsaras are present, and the blessed Hari dwells there, honoured with Prajapati in front."}},{"n":69,"text":"तत्र त्रीण्यग्निकुण्डानि येषां मध्ये च जाह्नवी ।\nप्रयागादभिनिष्क्रान्ता सर्वतीर्थपुरस्कृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are three fire-pits, in the middle of which the Jahnavi flows out of Prayaga, honoured by all fords."}},{"n":70,"text":"तपनस्य सुता तत्र त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुता ।\nयमुना गङ्गया सार्धं संगता लोकपावनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the daughter of the sun, famed in the three worlds, the world-purifying Yamuna, joins the Ganga."}},{"n":71,"text":"गङ्गायमुनयोर्मध्यं पृथिव्या जघनं स्मृतम् ।\nप्रयागं जघनस्यान्तमुपस्थमृषयो विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The region between the Ganga and the Yamuna is called the earth's hip, and the sages know Prayaga as the end of the hip, the loins."}},{"n":72,"text":"प्रयागं सप्रतिष्ठानं कम्बलाश्वतरौ तथा ।\nतीर्थं भोगवती चैव वेदी प्रोक्ता प्रजापतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prayaga with Pratishthana, Kambala and Ashvatara, and the ford Bhogavati are said to be Prajapati's altar."}},{"n":73,"text":"तत्र वेदाश्च यज्ञाश्च मूर्तिमन्तो युधिष्ठिर ।\nप्रजापतिमुपासन्ते ऋषयश्च महाव्रताः ।\nयजन्ते क्रतुभिर्देवास्तथा चक्रचरा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the Vedas and sacrifices stand embodied, Yudhishthira, and the sages of great vows worship Prajapati; the gods and those who go with the wheel perform sacrifices there with rites, O king."}},{"n":74,"text":"ततः पुण्यतमं नास्ति त्रिषु लोकेषु भारत ।\nप्रयागः सर्वतीर्थेभ्यः प्रभवत्यधिकं विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is nothing holier in the three worlds than that, O Bharata; Prayaga surpasses all fords, mighty one."}},{"n":75,"text":"श्रवणात्तस्य तीर्थस्य नामसंकीर्तनादपि ।\nमृत्तिकालम्भनाद्वापि नरः पापात्प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By hearing of that ford, by speaking its name, or by touching its earth, a man is freed from sin."}},{"n":76,"text":"तत्राभिषेकं यः कुर्यात्संगमे संशितव्रतः ।\nपुण्यं स फलमाप्नोति राजसूयाश्वमेधयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of sharp vows who bathes at that confluence gains the merit of the Rajasuya and the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":77,"text":"एषा यजनभूमिर्हि देवानामपि सत्कृता ।\nतत्र दत्तं सूक्ष्ममपि महद्भवति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is a sacrificial ground honoured even by the gods; even a small gift made there becomes great, O Bharata."}},{"n":78,"text":"न वेदवचनात्तात न लोकवचनादपि ।\nमतिरुत्क्रमणीया ते प्रयागमरणं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"My dear, neither because of a Vedic saying nor because of what people say should your mind turn away from dying at Prayaga."}},{"n":79,"text":"दश तीर्थसहस्राणि षष्टिकोट्यस्तथापराः ।\nयेषां सांनिध्यमत्रैव कीर्तितं कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ten thousand fords and sixty crores more are said to be present right here, joy of the Kurus."}},{"n":80,"text":"चातुर्वेदे च यत्पुण्यं सत्यवादिषु चैव यत् ।\nस्नात एव तदाप्नोति गङ्गायमुनसंगमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever merit there is in a master of the four Vedas and among truth-tellers, one gains merely by bathing at the confluence of the Ganga and Yamuna."}},{"n":81,"text":"तत्र भोगवती नाम वासुकेस्तीर्थमुत्तमम् ।\nतत्राभिषेकं यः कुर्यात्सोऽश्वमेधमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is the excellent ford of Vasuki named Bhogavati; one who bathes there gains the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":82,"text":"तत्र हंसप्रपतनं तीर्थं त्रैलोक्यविश्रुतम् ।\nदशाश्वमेधिकं चैव गङ्गायां कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is the ford Hamsaprapatana, famed in the three worlds, and Dashashvamedhika on the Ganga, joy of the Kurus."}},{"n":83,"text":"यत्र गङ्गा महाराज स देशस्तत्तपोवनम् ।\nसिद्धक्षेत्रं तु तज्ज्ञेयं गङ्गातीरसमाश्रितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever the Ganga is, great king, that region is an ascetic forest; know that land along the Ganga's bank to be a field of perfection."}},{"n":84,"text":"इदं सत्यं द्विजातीनां साधूनामात्मजस्य च ।\nसुहृदां च जपेत्कर्णे शिष्यस्यानुगतस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"This truth one should whisper in the ear of brahmins, good men, one's son, friends, and a devoted pupil."}},{"n":85,"text":"इदं धर्म्यमिदं पुण्यमिदं मेध्यमिदं सुखम् ।\nइदं स्वर्ग्यमिदं रम्यमिदं पावनमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is dharmic, holy, sacrificially pure, pleasant, leading to heaven, lovely, purifying and supreme."}},{"n":86,"text":"महर्षीणामिदं गुह्यं सर्वपापप्रमोचनम् ।\nअधीत्य द्विजमध्ये च निर्मलत्वमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the great sages' secret that frees from all sins; by reciting it among brahmins one attains purity."}},{"n":87,"text":"यश्चेदं शृणुयान्नित्यं तीर्थपुण्यं सदा शुचिः ।\nजातीः स स्मरते बह्वीर्नाकपृष्ठे च मोदते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who always listens to this merit of fords, ever pure, remembers many past births and rejoices in the highest heaven."}},{"n":88,"text":"गम्यान्यपि च तीर्थानि कीर्तितान्यगमानि च ।\nमनसा तानि गच्छेत सर्वतीर्थसमीक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the fords that can be reached and those that cannot, as described, one should visit in mind, taking in all the fords with the inner eye."}},{"n":89,"text":"एतानि वसुभिः साध्यैरादित्यैर्मरुदश्विभिः ।\nऋषिभिर्देवकल्पैश्च श्रितानि सुकृतैषिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These have been resorted to by the Vasus, Sadhyas, Adityas, Maruts, Ashvins, by sages and godlike beings who desire merit."}},{"n":90,"text":"एवं त्वमपि कौरव्य विधिनानेन सुव्रत ।\nव्रज तीर्थानि नियतः पुण्यं पुण्येन वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So you too, descendant of Kuru, of good vows, go to the fords by this method, restrained; merit grows by merit."}},{"n":91,"text":"भावितैः कारणैः पूर्वमास्तिक्याच्छ्रुतिदर्शनात् ।\nप्राप्यन्ते तानि तीर्थानि सद्भिः शिष्टानुदर्शिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Good men who follow the practice of the wise reach those fords by prior cultivated causes, belief in God and sight of the scriptures."}},{"n":92,"text":"नाव्रतो नाकृतात्मा च नाशुचिर्न च तस्करः ।\nस्नाति तीर्थेषु कौरव्य न च वक्रमतिर्नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is without vow, whose self is uncontrolled, who is impure, a thief, or crooked in mind does not bathe at the fords, descendant of Kuru."}},{"n":93,"text":"त्वया तु सम्यग्वृत्तेन नित्यं धर्मार्थदर्शिना ।\nपितरस्तारितास्तात सर्वे च प्रपितामहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear, by your right conduct and constant regard for dharma and prosperity you have already saved your ancestors and great-grandfathers."}},{"n":94,"text":"पितामहपुरोगाश्च देवाः सर्षिगणा नृप ।\nतव धर्मेण धर्मज्ञ नित्यमेवाभितोषिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods led by the Grandfather and the hosts of sages have always been pleased by your dharma, knower of dharma."}},{"n":95,"text":"अवाप्स्यसि च लोकान्वै वसूनां वासवोपम ।\nकीर्तिं च महतीं भीष्म प्राप्स्यसे भुवि शाश्वतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will gain the worlds of the Vasus, you who are like Indra, and, Bhishma, you will gain great, lasting fame on earth."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":96,"text":"एवमुक्त्वाभ्यनुज्ञाप्य पुलस्त्यो भगवानृषिः ।\nप्रीतः प्रीतेन मनसा तत्रैवान्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this and taken leave, the blessed sage Pulastya, pleased at heart, vanished right there."}},{"n":97,"text":"भीष्मश्च कुरुशार्दूल शास्त्रतत्त्वार्थदर्शिवान् ।\nपुलस्त्यवचनाच्चैव पृथिवीमनुचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Bhishma, tiger among the Kurus, who saw the true meaning of the scriptures, travelled over the earth by Pulastya's word."}},{"n":98,"text":"अनेन विधिना यस्तु पृथिवीं संचरिष्यति ।\nअश्वमेधशतस्याग्र्यं फलं प्रेत्य स भोक्ष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who travels the earth by this method will enjoy after death the best fruit of a hundred horse sacrifices."}},{"n":99,"text":"अतश्चाष्टगुणं पार्थ प्राप्स्यसे धर्ममुत्तमम् ।\nनेता च त्वमृषीन्यस्मात्तेन तेऽष्टगुणं फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And you, Partha, will gain eight times that highest dharma, because you will lead sages; for that reason your fruit will be eightfold."}},{"n":100,"text":"रक्षोगणावकीर्णानि तीर्थान्येतानि भारत ।\nन गतिर्विद्यतेऽन्यस्य त्वामृते कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"These fords are overrun by hosts of rakshasas, Bharata; no one but you has the means to go there, joy of the Kurus."}},{"n":101,"text":"इदं देवर्षिचरितं सर्वतीर्थार्थसंश्रितम् ।\nयः पठेत्कल्यमुत्थाय सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who rises at dawn and recites this account of the divine sages, which centres on all the fords, is freed from all sins."}},{"n":102,"text":"ऋषिमुख्याः सदा यत्र वाल्मीकिस्त्वथ काश्यपः ।\nआत्रेयस्त्वथ कौण्डिन्यो विश्वामित्रोऽथ गौतमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The chief sages always there are Valmiki, Kashyapa, Atreya, Kaundinya, Vishvamitra and Gautama,"}},{"n":103,"text":"असितो देवलश्चैव मार्कण्डेयोऽथ गालवः ।\nभरद्वाजो वसिष्ठश्च मुनिरुद्दालकस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Asita, Devala, Markandeya, Galava, Bharadvaja, Vasishtha, the muni Uddalaka,"}},{"n":104,"text":"शौनकः सह पुत्रेण व्यासश्च जपतां वरः ।\nदुर्वासाश्च मुनिश्रेष्ठो गालवश्च महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaunaka with his son, and Vyasa, best of those who recite, Durvasa, the best of munis, and the great ascetic Galava."}},{"n":105,"text":"एते ऋषिवराः सर्वे त्वत्प्रतीक्षास्तपोधनाः ।\nएभिः सह महाराज तीर्थान्येतान्यनुव्रज ॥","meaning":{"en":"All these best of sages, rich in austerity, are waiting for you. Go with them, great king, to these fords."}},{"n":106,"text":"एष वै लोमशो नाम देवर्षिरमितद्युतिः ।\nसमेष्यति त्वया चैव तेन सार्धमनुव्रज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here comes the divine sage Lomasha of boundless splendour; he will join you, so go with him."}},{"n":107,"text":"मया च सह धर्मज्ञ तीर्थान्येतान्यनुव्रज ।\nप्राप्स्यसे महतीं कीर्तिं यथा राजा महाभिषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go with me too, knower of dharma, to these fords; you will gain great fame, as King Mahabhisha did."}},{"n":108,"text":"यथा ययातिर्धर्मात्मा यथा राजा पुरूरवाः ।\nतथा त्वं कुरुशार्दूल स्वेन धर्मेण शोभसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Yayati of righteous soul and King Pururavas did, so you, tiger among the Kurus, shine by your own dharma."}},{"n":109,"text":"यथा भगीरथो राजा यथा रामश्च विश्रुतः ।\nतथा त्वं सर्वराजभ्यो भ्राजसे रश्मिवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As King Bhagiratha and renowned Rama did, you outshine all kings like the sun."}},{"n":110,"text":"यथा मनुर्यथेक्ष्वाकुर्यथा पूरुर्महायशाः ।\nयथा वैन्यो महातेजास्तथा त्वमपि विश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Manu, Ikshvaku, the greatly renowned Puru and the mighty Vainya were, so you too are famed."}},{"n":111,"text":"यथा च वृत्रहा सर्वान्सपत्नान्निर्दहत्पुरा ।\nतथा शत्रुक्षयं कृत्वा प्रजास्त्वं पालयिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the slayer of Vritra once burned all his rivals, so you will destroy your enemies and protect your subjects."}},{"n":112,"text":"स्वधर्मविजितामुर्वीं प्राप्य राजीवलोचन ।\nख्यातिं यास्यसि धर्मेण कार्तवीर्यार्जुनो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-eyed one, having regained the earth conquered by your own dharma, you will win fame by dharma, as Kartavirya Arjuna did."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":113,"text":"एवमाश्वास्य राजानं नारदो भगवानृषिः ।\nअनुज्ञाप्य महात्मानं तत्रैवान्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thus comforted the king, the blessed sage Narada took leave of the great soul and vanished right there."}},{"n":114,"text":"युधिष्ठिरोऽपि धर्मात्मा तमेवार्थं विचिन्तयन् ।\nतीर्थयात्राश्रयं पुण्यमृषीणां प्रत्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The righteous Yudhishthira, reflecting on that very matter, reported to the sages the holy practice of pilgrimage."}}]}]}